.TH START-VNC-SESSION.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom-setup 1.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start\-vnc\-session.sh \- start a control\-room VNC session and its discovery sidecar on a DAQ host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start\-vnc\-session.sh
.I session\-name display
.RB [ \-g
.IR WxH ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR depth ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs on the session host as the session account, normally via
.BR "crs\-remote start" .
If
.B "vncserver \-list"
already shows
.BI : display
it prints
.B SKIP
and exits 0.
Otherwise it runs
.PP
.EX
vncserver :DISPLAY \-geometry WxH \-depth D \-localhost yes \-xstartup XSTARTUP
.EE
.PP
.B "\-localhost yes"
makes the VNC server accept connections only from the loopback
interface; this line is where the control room's security model is
enforced, and the only way in from elsewhere is an ssh forward such as
.BR crs\-tunnel (1)
makes.
It holds only for sessions this script starts: a session started by
other means (a systemd
.B vncserver@
unit, or
.B vncserver
by hand) gets whatever the host's TigerVNC configuration says.
Check a running session with
.BR "ss \-ltn 'sport = :590N'" ;
the local address must be 127.0.0.1 or ::1.
Authentication within the host is the VNC password in
.IR ~/.vnc/passwd ,
which must exist beforehand.
.I XSTARTUP
is
.I $CRS_HOME/etc/xstartup
if executable, else
.IR ~/.vnc/xstartup ;
the shipped one starts XFCE with
.I ~/controlroom/bin
on the PATH.
.PP
It then starts
.BR vnc\-discovery\-responder.py (1)
in the background under the system
.B python3
(no virtual environment), records its pid, and prints
.BR OK .
If the responder is not installed it prints
.B WARN
and continues.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-g " WxH"
geometry; default
.B $CRS_GEOMETRY
or 1920x1080.
.TP
.BI \-d " depth"
colour depth; default
.B $CRS_DEPTH
or 24.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.crs/vnc\-responder\-:N.pid
sidecar pid.
.TP
.IR $CRS_HOME/log/vnc\- NAME .log ", " $CRS_HOME/log/vnc\-responder\- NAME .log
logs.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_HOME
install area (default
.IR ~/controlroom ).
.TP
.BR CRS_GEOMETRY ", " CRS_DEPTH
defaults for
.BR \-g ", " \-d .
.TP
.B CRS_ANNOUNCE_INTERVAL
seconds between the sidecar's unsolicited multicast announcements
(default 30; 0 disables).
.BR crs\-remote (1)
does not pass the configuration file's
.B discovery.announce_interval
here.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 started or already running; 1 usage error (including
.BR \-h ),
or non\-numeric display;
otherwise
.BR vncserver 's
status
.RB ( "set \-e" ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
start\-vnc\-session.sh shift\-main 2 \-g 1920x1080
CRS_ANNOUNCE_INTERVAL=0 start\-vnc\-session.sh dcs\-main 1
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stop\-vnc\-session.sh (1),
.BR status\-vnc\-session.sh (1),
.BR vnc\-discovery\-responder.py (1),
.BR crs\-remote (1),
.BR vncserver (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group.
